From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: repatches <repatches@kimono.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:17:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mobile: Connect from a Kimono link and go straight to Kimono
 sign-in

Nobody types, sees or edits the server address, and opening the app goes
directly to Kimono's sign-in sheet instead of an Immich sign-in screen.

Must survive upstream changes:
- lib/kimono/kimono_connect.dart owns the address: saved from the
  kimono-photos://connect?server=<https origin> link (accepted only while
  signed out; http only in debug builds) or the KIMONO_PHOTOS_SERVER
  dart-define. It is stored in StoreKey.serverUrl, which upstream's own
  validateServerUrl also writes.
- The router (main.dart deep link builder) handles the connect link before
  any other kimono-photos:// link.
- The sign-in screen has no address field, no address text, no Back and no
  Settings button. With an address it resolves the server and, when OAuth
  is on, starts OAuth immediately (spinner meanwhile). Without one it says
  to open Photos from Kimono. On failure: "Try again".
- Before opening the sign-in sheet by itself it waits until the app is the
  active foreground app (KimonoConnect.untilForeground): iOS rejects the
  sheet otherwise (ASWebAuthenticationSession error 3), and a connect link
  arrives while iOS is still dismissing its "Open in Kimono Photos?" prompt.
- Kimono is the only way in: the sign-in screen has no email and password
  form at all, even if the server allows passwords. If Kimono sign-in fails
  or is cancelled the screen offers "Sign in with Kimono" again; if the
  server has OAuth off it says Kimono sign-in is off for Photos.
- After a person taps Sign out (the account sheet sets
  KimonoConnect.signedOut) the screen waits on the Kimono button instead of
  bouncing straight back in. AuthService.logout must NOT set it: the app also
  signs out by itself (start-up with no saved session, password change), and
  the first launch from the Portal must still go straight to Kimono.
- "Open in browser" is never offered on a photo: it would show the
  server address in the browser.
- The address is not shown anywhere else: removed from the account sheet's
  server info, and the Networking settings section is hidden.
- Immich's hidden demo-server shortcuts on the logo are removed.
- The login form otherwise follows upstream: its translations (context.t),
  context.mounted guards and post-sign-in steps (gallery permission, sync,
  featureMessageService.markSeen, TabShellRoute) are upstream's, with
  oAuthLogin returning whether it signed in so the screen can offer it again.

diff --git a/mobile/lib/kimono/kimono_connect.dart b/mobile/lib/kimono/kimono_connect.dart
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..76cc435
--- /dev/null
+++ b/mobile/lib/kimono/kimono_connect.dart
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+import 'dart:async';
+
+import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart';
+import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart';
+import 'package:immich_mobile/domain/models/store.model.dart';
+import 'package:immich_mobile/entities/store.entity.dart';
+
+/// Where Kimono Photos lives, and whether to go straight to Kimono sign-in.
+///
+/// The address comes from the `kimono-photos://connect?server=…` link the
+/// Kimono Portal opens on this phone (or is baked in with
+/// `--dart-define=KIMONO_PHOTOS_SERVER=…`). It is kept, never shown, and
+/// can't be typed in: there is no address field anywhere in the app.
+abstract final class KimonoConnect {
+  static const _builtIn = String.fromEnvironment('KIMONO_PHOTOS_SERVER');
+
+  /// Bumped when a connect link arrives, so an open sign-in screen follows it.
+  static final requests = ValueNotifier<int>(0);
+
+  /// True after someone taps Sign out, so the sign-in screen waits for them
+  /// instead of sending them straight back into Kimono. Only that button sets
+  /// it: the app also signs out on its own (e.g. at start-up with no saved
+  /// session), and those must not stop the automatic sign-in.
+  static bool signedOut = false;
+
+  static String? get server {
+    final saved = Store.tryGet(StoreKey.serverUrl);
+    if (saved != null && saved.isNotEmpty) {
+      return saved;
+    }
+    return _builtIn.isEmpty ? null : _builtIn;
+  }
+
+  /// Waits until the app is the active, foreground app. iOS refuses to show
+  /// the sign-in sheet otherwise (ASWebAuthenticationSession error 3), and a
+  /// connect link arrives while iOS is still dismissing its "Open in…?" prompt.
+  static Future<void> untilForeground() async {
+    final binding = WidgetsBinding.instance;
+    if (binding.lifecycleState != AppLifecycleState.resumed) {
+      final resumed = Completer<void>();
+      final listener = AppLifecycleListener(
+        onResume: () {
+          if (!resumed.isCompleted) {
+            resumed.complete();
+          }
+        },
+      );
+      await resumed.future.timeout(const Duration(seconds: 30), onTimeout: () {});
+      listener.dispose();
+    }
+    await binding.endOfFrame;
+  }
+
+  static bool isConnectLink(Uri uri) => uri.scheme == 'kimono-photos' && uri.host == 'connect';
+
+  /// Saves the address from a connect link. Plain http only in debug builds.
+  static Future<bool> accept(Uri link) async {
+    final raw = link.queryParameters['server'];
+    final uri = raw == null ? null : Uri.tryParse(raw);
+    if (uri == null || uri.host.isEmpty) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    if (uri.scheme != 'https' && !(kDebugMode && uri.scheme == 'http')) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    await Store.put(StoreKey.serverUrl, uri.origin);
+    signedOut = false;
+    requests.value++;
+    return true;
+  }
+}
